;; THE RUN-ERA LEDGER -- the seam file of EPIC-run-era.md.
;;
;; One row per (run-id, check-id): what a named check said about a named WM run,
;; with a pointer to the artifact it said it from. This file is the analog of
;; the PLoP-2026 empirics pipeline's `empirics/field-desk-loss.json`: the run
;; store under `runs/` is upstream of it, generated figures and sections are
;; downstream of it, and nothing downstream may claim more than this file holds.
;;
;; APPEND-ONLY, AND MECHANICALLY SO. Rows are written by exactly one API --
;; `run_era_ledger.bb`'s `append-row!` (CLI: `--append`). This file is never
;; hand-edited. Each row carries `:row/sha`, a SHA-256 over that row's authored
;; fields chained to the previous row's `:row/sha` (genesis string "genesis"),
;; and `:ledger/head-sha` is the last row's sha. So an in-place edit of a row
;; already written, or a truncation of the tail, is a VALIDATION DEFECT rather
;; than an honour-system violation: `bb run_era_ledger.bb --check` fails.
;;
;; SCHEMA-IN-FILE. `:ledger/schema` below is the only copy of the row shape;
;; the validator reads it from here, so file and validator cannot drift (the
;; tension-ledger.edn discipline, u41_tension_ledger.bb).
;;
;; HONEST STORE RULE. A check that had nothing to read deposits a row with
;; `:row/verdict :typed-absence` and a `:row/notes` saying what was missing --
;; never silence, and never a green. The validator refuses a `:typed-absence`
;; row with blank notes.
;;
;; STATUS IS A FOLD. There is no status field anywhere in this file. A run's
;; status is the fold of its rows against the declared check catalogue
;; (`bb run_era_ledger.bb --report`), and a check's history is the fold of its
;; rows ordered by run -- the time-correlation the epic exists for.

